lib/IO/K8s/Role/Resource.pm:171 -- to_json encodes with utf8 => 1
(bytes), but from_json uses state $json = JSON::MaybeXS->new without
utf8. Class->from_json($obj->to_json) therefore reads UTF-8 bytes as
characters.

Repro (measured): ConfigMap with data => { greet => "uber-with-umlaut" }
roundtrips to mojibake (length 5 instead of 4), with NO error raised.
t/05_utf8.t only covers the instance path ($k8s->json_to_object), not
this one.

Silent data mutation. Fix sketch: JSON::MaybeXS->new(utf8 => 1) in
from_json, symmetric to _build_json -- decide whether character-string
input must stay accepted (decode-tolerant) and say so in POD.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer (extend t/05).

Fixed: from_json decodes with utf8 => 1. Decision: strict bytes, no decode tolerance -- a shim would make from_json more permissive than json_to_object, which has always been byte-oriented. Recorded in the new =method from_json POD. Tests: t/05_utf8.t.
